cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spintrack, please cite it as below, and FicTrac, whose output it reproduces."
type: software
title: "spintrack: track the rotation of a spherical treadmill from video"
authors:
  - family-names: Lam
    given-names: Thomas Ka Chung
    email: thomas.lam@epfl.ch
    affiliation: "EPFL, Neuroengineering Laboratory"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NeLy-EPFL/spintrack"
url: "https://nely-epfl.github.io/spintrack/"
abstract: >-
  Track the 3D rotation of a spherical treadmill (trackball) from video and
  reconstruct the animal's fictive path. spintrack streams FicTrac's records in
  FicTrac's line format and writes them to Parquet, and estimates the rotation
  photometrically against an accumulated surface map of the ball.
keywords:
  - trackball
  - spherical treadmill
  - fictive path
  - Drosophila
  - tracking
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: "FicTrac: a visual method for tracking spherical motion and generating fictive animal paths"
    authors:
      - family-names: Moore
        given-names: Richard J. D.
      - family-names: Taylor
        given-names: Gavin J.
      - family-names: Paulk
        given-names: Angelique C.
      - family-names: Pearson
        given-names: Thomas
      - family-names: van Swinderen
        given-names: Bruno
      - family-names: Srinivasan
        given-names: Mandyam V.
    journal: "Journal of Neuroscience Methods"
    volume: 225
    start: 106
    end: 119
    year: 2014
    doi: 10.1016/j.jneumeth.2014.01.010
